<footer class="notes">
  <p>Pay is total fiscal-year 2025: regular pay plus overtime plus other pay such as lump sums and retroactive raises. Base salary is shown beside it. A large gap might mean a one-off payout. Base salary is the annual rate at the end of the fiscal year, so it can be higher than what was actually paid when someone got a raise or started partway through the year.</p>
  <p>Source: NYC Office of Payroll Administration, <a href="https://data.cityofnewyork.us/d/k397-673e">Citywide Payroll Data (Fiscal Year)</a> plus research on how you get each job, ideally from something like a DCAS exam notice.</p>
  <p>Not affiliated with the City of New York. Everything is as of October 2026. Job postings are cited for their requirements, and most have since closed.</p>
